# Requirements

## Hypotheses

### H1: Lags below 225 deg at 2.1 Hz give more forward travel

WHEN c2 and c3 carry sines at 2.1 Hz with c3 lagging c2 by 200 deg and c0, c1, c4 are 0, THE system SHALL reach x of at least 0.27 m while heading stays within 20 deg of the start.

```prediction
# relies on: R8, R7
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.27, 0.45]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
f = 2.1
phi = 200
c4a = 0

[[prediction]]
id = "P2"
measurement = "heading"
range = [-20.0, 20.0]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
f = 2.1
phi = 200
c4a = 0
```

Notes: three trials: lag 200 deg, lag 180 deg, and lag 225 deg with c4 in phase with c2 at amplitude 0.5 (c4a).

Result of H1 (E1): 2.1 Hz lag 200, c4 off gave x 0.294 m, y 0.113 m, heading 10.6 deg. Lag 180 gave x 0.320, heading 41.8. Lag 225 with c4 in phase at 0.5 gave x 0.312, heading 24.9. Verdict partly.

### H2: Anti-phase c4 holds heading down while lag 200 to 210 keeps x near 0.3 m

WHEN c2 and c3 carry 2.1 Hz sines with c3 lagging by 200 deg and c4 carries the c2 sine at amplitude -0.3, THE system SHALL reach x of at least 0.3 m with heading within 20 deg of the start.

```prediction
